$schema: https://usm.dev/schema/v1.json
$id: smith-gray/secret-transport
$type: feature
$version: 1
$last_updated: "2026-09-22"
summary: |
  Transport is how a secret gets from where it was created to where it is used — across
  environments, clouds, agents, and multi-agent protocol buses (MCP, A2A) — carrying only folders
  and tokens. No unwrap occurs during transport, so the journey is the safe part and every hop can
  be untrusted.
$system: smith-gray/system
$service: smith-gray/sidecar
status: in-progress
intent: |
  Agentic systems route credentials through many hops, and each hop is traditionally a new
  exposure. Making the transport artefacts inert (ciphertext folders) and the authority artefact
  harmless (tokens) decouples movement from risk: a secret can be copied anywhere, and the only
  place it becomes real is a sidecar with a valid token at the destination.
flows:
  - id: agent-to-agent
    name: Transport a secret between agents
    description: Agent A creates a secret; Agent B uses it, with neither transcript containing plaintext.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: receive
        target: Agent A creates a secret and receives a token and folder path.
      - id: s2
        action: send
        target: Agent A passes the folder path and token to Agent B through the agent bus.
      - id: s3
        action: observe
        target: No unwrap occurs in transit; the folder is inert.
      - id: s4
        action: send
        target: Agent B presents the token to its local sidecar to use the secret.
      - id: s5
        action: observe
        target: Neither Agent A's nor Agent B's transcript contains plaintext.
  - id: cross-environment
    name: Transport a secret across environments
    description: A folder is synced or copied to another environment and used there under a new token.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: send
        target: >-
          The folder is copied to the destination environment via git, an object store, or
          artefacts.
      - id: s2
        action: observe
        target: No key material travels with it and no unwrap occurs.
      - id: s3
        action: transmit
        target: A token scoped to the destination audience is minted.
      - id: s4
        action: observe
        target: >-
          The destination sidecar can now resolve; the source's token cannot be used at the
          destination.
contracts:
  - id: transport-is-inert
    description: Moving a secret must not require or reveal key material.
    must_have:
      - Transport carries folders and tokens only
      - No unwrap occurs during transport
      - Compromise of a transport channel yields ciphertext and tokens, not values
  - id: tokens-bounded-to-audience
    description: A token valid in one environment is not automatically valid in another.
    must_have:
      - aud binds the token to its intended resolver or environment
      - A token used outside its audience is denied
      - Cross-environment use requires a new token
  - id: transcripts-stay-clean
    description: Agent-to-agent handoff leaves no plaintext in any transcript, log, or tool call.
    must_have:
      - Handoff payloads contain only paths and tokens
      - The two-agent demo asserts no transcript contains plaintext
      - Tool-call arguments never carry values
tests:
  - id: two-agent-demo-no-plaintext
    flow: agent-to-agent
    setup:
      agent_a: creator
      agent_b: consumer
      secret_value: demo-secret
    expect:
      - assertion: Agent A's transcript contains no plaintext
      - assertion: Agent B's transcript contains no plaintext
      - assertion: Agent B successfully used the secret
    contracts:
      - transcripts-stay-clean
      - transport-is-inert
  - id: cross-environment-token-rejected
    flow: cross-environment
    setup:
      source_aud: env-staging
      destination: env-production
    expect:
      - assertion: the source token is denied at the destination
      - assertion: a destination-scoped token succeeds
    contracts:
      - tokens-bounded-to-audience
  - id: intercepted-transport-yields-nothing
    flow: cross-environment
    setup:
      capture_transport: true
    expect:
      - assertion: captured payloads contain no plaintext
      - assertion: captured tokens cannot be used without a reachable sidecar and key authority
    contracts:
      - transport-is-inert
decisions:
  - id: transport-is-the-differentiator
    decision: >-
      Differentiate on transport — folders and tokens that agents create and move through arbitrary
      flows — rather than on use-time brokering alone.
    rationale: >-
      The competitive analysis in the blueprint notes that broker and proxy patterns already keep
      credentials out of model context at use time. Transport is the gap — the ability to move
      secrets freely through agentic flows with a stable interface that can later grow a hardware
      root of trust.
    status: accepted
  - id: bus-agnostic-payload
    decision: Carry only folder URIs and tokens over MCP, A2A, and other agent buses.
    rationale: >-
      Bus payloads are logged, cached, and inspected by third parties; keeping them inert makes
      every one of those observers harmless.
    status: accepted
implementation:
  primary: pkg/sidecar/server.go
  test_code: test/e2e/two_agent_demo_test.go
  test_code_status: manual
see_also:
  - smith-gray/encrypted-folder
  - smith-gray/capability-token
  - smith-gray/mcp-server
